.Dd August 16, 2026
.Dt RCGC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rcgc
.Nd remove leftover broken symlinks
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm rcgc
.Op Fl afhnqVv
.Op Fl d Ar dir
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This program will find symlinks in
.Pa $HOME
that point into a dotfiles directory but would not be listed by
.Xr lsrc 1 .
Typically such links are the result of deleting or renaming a dotfile.
.Pp
The
.Nm
program finds those links, lists them, and then asks once whether to
remove the whole batch.
.Pp
By default,
.Nm
only searches within
.Pa $HOME
subdirectories that are managed by rcm--that is, those
that
.Xr rcup 1
would create and that
.Xr rcdn 1
would remove.
If an entire subdirectory is deleted from a dotfiles directory, pass
.Fl a
to broaden the scan to include all of
.Pa $HOME ;
otherwise the stale links pointing into the deleted directory will not be
detected.
.Pp
When a link is removed and it was the last entry in its directory, that
directory is also removed.
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width "-d DIR"
.It Fl a
search all of
.Pa $HOME
rather than only the directories implied by the dotfiles repository layout.
.It Fl d Ar DIR
remove links pointing into
.Ar DIR
instead of those named by
.Va DOTFILES_DIRS .
This can be specified multiple times.
.It Fl f
do not prompt to delete links; assume a response of
.Qq y .
.It Fl h
show usage instructions.
.It Fl n
do not prompt to delete links; assume a response of
.Qq n .
.It Fl q
decrease verbosity. Implies
.Fl n.
Use with
.Fl f
to remove links quietly.
.It Fl v
increase verbosity. This can be repeated for extra verbosity.
.It Fl V
show the version number.
.El
.
.Sh IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
Because
.Xr rcup 1
cannot create a link whose target path contains a newline, or a link with a
relative target path, these links are always left alone even if they are broken,
as they are assumed to have been created manually.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ".Ev RCRC"
.It Ev RCRC
User configuration file. Defaults to
.Pa ~/.rcrc .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Pa ~/.rcrc
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl rcgc
.Dl rcgc -qf
.Dl rcgc -a
.Dl rcgc -d ~/corporate-dotfiles
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lsrc 1 ,
.Xr mkrc 1 ,
.Xr rcdn 1 ,
.Xr rcup 1 ,
.Xr rcrc 5 ,
.Xr rcm 7
